title: The Assembly Agenda Committee Discusses Reconvocation
subtitle: Staal's new lease on life?
view-if: chancellor = "Staal" and staal_time and (next_reichstag_time - 1) == rubicon_time
on-arrival: {!
if (((Q.army_strength*Q.army_militancy + Q.heartland_police_strength*Q.heartland_police_militancy)*2 < Q.total_force && Q.heartland_leader == "Staal") || (Q.army_strength*Q.army_militancy)*2 < (Q.total_force + Q.heartland_police_strength*Q.heartland_police_militancy*Q.heartland_police_loyalty) && Q.heartland_leader != "Staal") {
  Q.staal_reichstag_smart = 1;
}
if (Q.staal_economy_time) Q.staal_reichstag_smart = 1;
!}
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/reichstag.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
go-to: schleicher_reichstag_menu

= Assembly Reconvocation Decision

The Assembly, which Staal had urged to reconvene as soon as possible, is set to revisit its earlier decision to reconvene next week. The outcome will determine when the inevitable confrontation between the Staal cabinet and a hostile parliament will occur. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> spokesmen support reconvening the chamber as planned, while the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>'s spokesman, Bram Frask, has adopted a noticeably less confrontational tone.

Frask shares many of Crowde’s concerns about [+ royalist_leader +]’s all-or-nothing stance and fears that a new election would bring disastrous <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> losses. Yet even figures like Standerton believe they need more time, and the top <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leaders have pushed Frask to propose delaying the reconvening until the cabinet can present its budget in a few months.

[? if not staal_economy_time: Nevertheless, Staal appears determined to continue his unwise strategy of offense—pushing for an immediate showdown with the Assembly in hopes that [+ royalist_leader +] will shift position to avoid new elections or, failing that, that DuFour will grant him an emergency decree. ?][? if staal_economy_time: It is expected that Staal will reverse his earlier, unwise strategy of confrontation and instead lend his support to Frask's proposal. ?]

In any case, there’s enough support among the other parties to pass Frask’s motion to extend the recess, rendering our vote irrelevant.

@schleicher_reichstag_menu

- @reichstag_1
- @reichstag_2

@reichstag_1
title: Frask's proposal is shot down!
view-if: not staal_reichstag_smart
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_reichstag_time = Q.rubicon_time + 1;
Q.next_reichstag_week = Q.week + 1;
Q.next_reichstag_month = Q.month;
Q.next_reichstag_year = Q.year;

Q.staal_explode = 1;

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_month > 12) {
  Q.next_reichstag_month -= 12;
  Q.next_reichstag_year += 1;
}
!}

As expected, the objections raised by Staal’s spokesman—acting on direct orders—have sunk the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> motion. In response, the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> has introduced a compromise: a one-week extension of the recess to allow for further negotiations. 

Goodryke’s scheme has become considerably easier, as Staal is now forced to test the President’s support by requesting a decree to dissolve the Assembly and postpone elections. But if DuFour denies the request, the question becomes unavoidable: who would succeed him? Goodryke? Gallax?

Staal has squandered a critical opportunity to salvage his cabinet—and perhaps the Commonwealth itself. Had the elections been postponed just a few months, his position would likely have improved significantly. He stood to gain from the launch of Gereke’s public works program and the natural recovery of the global economy. Meanwhile, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, with no upcoming state elections to boost morale, would have been increasingly vulnerable to internal collapse—driven by mounting dissatisfaction with [+ royalist_leader +] and the disintegration of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>.

None of this is to be.

@reichstag_2
title: Staal approves Frask's proposal.
subtitle: This is a turning point.
unavailable-subtitle: Staal remains committed to his delusions.
choose-if: staal_reichstag_smart
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_reichstag_time = Q.rubicon_time + 9;
Q.next_reichstag_week = Q.week + 9;
Q.next_reichstag_month = Q.month;
Q.next_reichstag_year = Q.year;

Q.staal_explode = 0;

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_month > 12) {
  Q.next_reichstag_month -= 12;
  Q.next_reichstag_year += 1;
}
!}

[? if not staal_economy_time: However, Staal, having learned about Frask's plans to delay the Assembly's reconvocation, has had a sudden change of heart. A new round of war games—this time not rigged—has revealed that the Commonwealth Army cannot survive fighting against all paramilitaries[? if heartland_leader == "Staal":, even with the Heartland police?][? if heartland_leader != "Staal":, and the Heartland police force as well?]. Despite his efforts to strengthen the army with streetfighting equipment and training, the limited but well-trained force remains unable to withstand being heavily outnumbered. ?][? if staal_economy_time: Staal, seeking to benefit from his public works program before calling for confrontation in the Assembly that'll likely lead to new elections, has decided that Frask's proposal is most prudent. ?]

[? if not staal_economy_time: The chancellor makes it clear that he still hopes [+ royalist_leader +] might have a sudden change of heart, but with his backup plan no longer viable, he pushes for the adoption of Frask's proposal. ?] The Assembly is now adjourned until [+ next_reichstag_month : month +] [+ next_reichstag_year +], Week [+ next_reichstag_week +], and Staal is expected to unveil his public works program during this time.